---
// Pulse terms of service (app beta, waitlist and this website).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../../styles/pulse.css';
import { site, mailto } from '../../config/site';
const email = site.contact.email;
const mail = mailto(email, 'Pulse terms');
---
<Base title="Pulse terms of service" description="The terms for using the Pulse app beta, the Pulse waitlist and this website." image="/og/pulse.png">
  <div class="pulse">
    <article class="container p-page">
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pulse</span>
        <h1>Pulse terms of service</h1>
        <p class="muted">Last updated: 22 November 2026</p>

        <p>
          These terms apply when you use Pulse ("the app"), join the Pulse waitlist or use this website. Pulse is made by
          Nifty Games Studios ("we"). By using the app, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use it.
          Questions: <a href={mail}>{email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who can use Pulse</h2>
        <p>Pulse is for adults (18 and over), such as medical graduates, interns and doctors preparing for exams.</p>

        <h2>2. Early beta</h2>
        <p>
          Pulse is in early beta. Features may change, break or be removed, and some content is still being reviewed.
          We give the beta to you as it is, and we may pause or end it at any time. Your progress may be reset during the beta.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Exam revision only, not medical advice</h2>
        <p>
          Pulse is a revision tool. It is not medical advice, and it must not be used to diagnose or treat patients or to make
          clinical decisions. Cards and questions can contain mistakes. Always check your standard textbooks and current
          guidelines. If you find something wrong, use the report button on the card.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Your account and use</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You can use the app without an account. If you sign in with Google, keep your sign-in details safe.</li>
          <li>You are responsible for what you do with your account, including friends and leaderboard features.</li>
          <li>Pick a name and picture that are not offensive or someone else's.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. What you must not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Copy, scrape, resell or share the cards, questions or pictures, in whole or in large parts.</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer the app or interfere with how it works, or with other people's use of it.</li>
          <li>Cheat on leaderboards, harass other users or use the app for anything unlawful.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may remove accounts or access that break these rules.</p>

        <h2>6. Ownership</h2>
        <p>
          The app, its design, cards, questions and pictures belong to Nifty Games Studios or are used with permission, and
          are protected by law. You get a personal, non-transferable right to use the app for your own revision. Some
          pictures come from other creators under open licences, and the credit is shown with each picture.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your feedback</h2>
        <p>
          If you send us feedback or a report, you allow us to use it to improve Pulse without paying you. Please do not send
          anything private or confidential about patients.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          How we use your information is explained in the <a href="/pulse/privacy/">Pulse privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Paid features</h2>
        <p>The beta is free. If we add paid features later, we will tell you clearly before you pay, and these terms will be updated.</p>

        <h2>10. Our responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent the law allows, we are not responsible for losses that come from using the app, from mistakes in
          content, from the app being unavailable, or from lost progress. Nothing in these terms limits any right you have
          under law that cannot be limited.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes and ending</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms. We will change the date above and, for important changes, tell you in the app. If you keep
          using Pulse after a change, you accept it. You can stop using the app at any time, and you can ask us to delete your
          data by emailing <a href={mail}>{email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India.</p>

        <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a href="/pulse/">Back to Pulse</a></p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
